{"question_text": {"Histology": [{"id": "1", "question": "১) Which of the following structure is composed of actin subunits and allow motility and most contractile activity in cells?", "option1": "microtubule", "option2": "microfilament", "option3": "intermediate filament", "option4": "All of them", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p data-start=\"206\" data-end=\"394\" class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\">The correct answer is<span> </span><strong data-start=\"228\" data-end=\"245\">microfilament</strong>. Microfilaments are composed of<span> </span><strong data-start=\"278\" data-end=\"287\">actin</strong><span> </span>and are responsible for<span> </span><strong data-start=\"312\" data-end=\"393\">cell motility, muscle contraction, cytokinesis, and maintenance of cell shape</strong>.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"396\" data-end=\"635\">\r\n<li data-start=\"396\" data-end=\"493\">\r\n<p data-start=\"398\" data-end=\"493\"><strong data-start=\"398\" data-end=\"414\">Microtubules</strong><span> </span>– Made of tubulin; involved in cilia, flagella, and mitotic spindle formation.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"494\" data-end=\"562\">\r\n<p data-start=\"496\" data-end=\"562\"><strong data-start=\"496\" data-end=\"522\">Intermediate filaments</strong><span> </span>– Provide mechanical strength to cells.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"563\" data-end=\"635\">\r\n<p data-start=\"565\" data-end=\"635\"><strong data-start=\"565\" data-end=\"580\">All of them</strong><span> </span>– Incorrect because only microfilaments contain actin.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"637\" data-end=\"659\"><strong data-start=\"637\" data-end=\"659\">High-yield points:</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"660\" data-end=\"821\">\r\n<li data-start=\"660\" data-end=\"717\">\r\n<p data-start=\"662\" data-end=\"717\"><strong data-start=\"662\" data-end=\"717\">Microfilament → Actin → Cell movement + contraction</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"718\" data-end=\"772\">\r\n<p data-start=\"720\" data-end=\"772\"><strong data-start=\"720\" data-end=\"772\">Microtubule → Tubulin → Spindle, cilia, flagella</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"773\" data-end=\"821\">\r\n<p data-start=\"775\" data-end=\"821\"><strong data-start=\"775\" data-end=\"821\">Intermediate filament → Structural support</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>"}, {"id": "2", "question": "২) Which organelle is responsible for protein synthesis?", "option1": "ribosome", "option2": "lysosome", "option3": "golgi bodies", "option4": "peroxisome", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p data-start=\"961\" data-end=\"1083\" class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\">The correct answer is<span> </span><strong data-start=\"983\" data-end=\"995\">ribosome</strong>. Ribosomes are the sites of<span> </span><strong data-start=\"1024\" data-end=\"1039\">translation</strong>, where mRNA is used to synthesize proteins.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1085\" data-end=\"1243\">\r\n<li data-start=\"1085\" data-end=\"1126\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1087\" data-end=\"1126\"><strong data-start=\"1087\" data-end=\"1099\">Lysosome</strong><span> </span>– Intracellular digestion.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1127\" data-end=\"1183\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1129\" data-end=\"1183\"><strong data-start=\"1129\" data-end=\"1145\">Golgi bodies</strong><span> </span>– Protein modification and packaging.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1184\" data-end=\"1243\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1186\" data-end=\"1243\"><strong data-start=\"1186\" data-end=\"1200\">Peroxisome</strong><span> </span>– Fatty acid oxidation and detoxification.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"1245\" data-end=\"1267\"><strong data-start=\"1245\" data-end=\"1267\">High-yield points:</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1268\" data-end=\"1394\">\r\n<li data-start=\"1268\" data-end=\"1302\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1270\" data-end=\"1302\"><strong data-start=\"1270\" data-end=\"1302\">Ribosome → Protein synthesis</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1303\" data-end=\"1355\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1305\" data-end=\"1355\"><strong data-start=\"1305\" data-end=\"1355\">RER → Synthesis of secretory/membrane proteins</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1356\" data-end=\"1394\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1358\" data-end=\"1394\"><strong data-start=\"1358\" data-end=\"1394\">Golgi → Modification + packaging</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>"}, {"id": "3", "question": "৩) Where does rRNA transcription and ribosomal subunits assembly occur?", "option1": "Ribosome", "option2": "Nucleolus", "option3": "Golgi apparatus", "option4": "Endoplasmic reticulum", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p data-start=\"1549\" data-end=\"1669\" class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\">The correct answer is<span> </span><strong data-start=\"1571\" data-end=\"1584\">nucleolus</strong>. The nucleolus is the site of<span> </span><strong data-start=\"1615\" data-end=\"1668\">rRNA synthesis and assembly of ribosomal subunits</strong>.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1671\" data-end=\"1844\">\r\n<li data-start=\"1671\" data-end=\"1739\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1673\" data-end=\"1739\"><strong data-start=\"1673\" data-end=\"1685\">Ribosome</strong><span> </span>– Site of protein synthesis, not ribosome production.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1740\" data-end=\"1785\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1742\" data-end=\"1785\"><strong data-start=\"1742\" data-end=\"1761\">Golgi apparatus</strong><span> </span>– Protein modification.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1786\" data-end=\"1844\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1788\" data-end=\"1844\"><strong data-start=\"1788\" data-end=\"1813\">Endoplasmic reticulum</strong><span> </span>– Protein and lipid synthesis.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"1846\" data-end=\"1868\"><strong data-start=\"1846\" data-end=\"1868\">High-yield points:</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1869\" data-end=\"1920\">\r\n<li data-start=\"1869\" data-end=\"1920\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1871\" data-end=\"1920\"><strong data-start=\"1871\" data-end=\"1920\">Nucleolus → rRNA + ribosomal subunit assembly</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>"}, {"id": "4", "question": "৪) Which is not true about Barr bodies?", "option1": "occurs during interphase", "option2": "present in sex cell of female", "option3": "heterochromatin plano convex body", "option4": "lies beneath nuclear membrane", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p data-start=\"2066\" data-end=\"2252\" class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\">The correct answer is<span> </span><strong data-start=\"2088\" data-end=\"2121\">present in sex cell of female</strong>. Barr bodies represent an<span> </span><strong data-start=\"2148\" data-end=\"2173\">inactive X chromosome</strong><span> </span>and are present in<span> </span><strong data-start=\"2193\" data-end=\"2221\">somatic cells of females</strong>, not in mature female gametes.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"2254\" data-end=\"2384\">\r\n<li data-start=\"2254\" data-end=\"2292\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2256\" data-end=\"2292\"><strong data-start=\"2256\" data-end=\"2284\">Occurs during interphase</strong><span> </span>– True.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2293\" data-end=\"2340\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2295\" data-end=\"2340\"><strong data-start=\"2295\" data-end=\"2332\">Heterochromatin plano-convex body</strong><span> </span>– True.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2341\" data-end=\"2384\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2343\" data-end=\"2384\"><strong data-start=\"2343\" data-end=\"2376\">Lies beneath nuclear membrane</strong><span> </span>– True.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"2386\" data-end=\"2408\"><strong data-start=\"2386\" data-end=\"2408\">High-yield points:</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"2409\" data-end=\"2549\">\r\n<li data-start=\"2409\" data-end=\"2448\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2411\" data-end=\"2448\"><strong data-start=\"2411\" data-end=\"2448\">Barr body = inactive X chromosome</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2449\" data-end=\"2491\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2451\" data-end=\"2491\"><strong data-start=\"2451\" data-end=\"2491\">Female somatic cells → one Barr body</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2492\" data-end=\"2549\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2494\" data-end=\"2549\"><strong data-start=\"2494\" data-end=\"2549\">Number of Barr bodies = Number of X chromosomes − 1</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>"}, {"id": "5", "question": "৫) Which of the following degrades denatured or otherwise nonfunctional polypeptides?", "option1": "Proteasomes", "option2": "ribosome", "option3": "lysosome", "option4": "peroxisome", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p data-start=\"2713\" data-end=\"2863\" class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\">The correct answer is<span> </span><strong data-start=\"2735\" data-end=\"2750\">proteasomes</strong>. Proteasomes degrade<span> </span><strong data-start=\"2772\" data-end=\"2821\">damaged, misfolded, or nonfunctional proteins</strong><span> </span>through the ubiquitin–proteasome pathway.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"2865\" data-end=\"3027\">\r\n<li data-start=\"2865\" data-end=\"2900\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2867\" data-end=\"2900\"><strong data-start=\"2867\" data-end=\"2879\">Ribosome</strong><span> </span>– Protein synthesis.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2901\" data-end=\"2978\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2903\" data-end=\"2978\"><strong data-start=\"2903\" data-end=\"2915\">Lysosome</strong><span> </span>– Digestion of extracellular material and cellular components.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2979\" data-end=\"3027\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2981\" data-end=\"3027\"><strong data-start=\"2981\" data-end=\"2995\">Peroxisome</strong><span> </span>– Oxidation and detoxification.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"3029\" data-end=\"3051\"><strong data-start=\"3029\" data-end=\"3051\">High-yield points:</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3052\" data-end=\"3144\">\r\n<li data-start=\"3052\" data-end=\"3090\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3054\" data-end=\"3090\"><strong data-start=\"3054\" data-end=\"3090\">Proteasome → Protein degradation</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3091\" data-end=\"3144\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3093\" data-end=\"3144\"><strong data-start=\"3093\" data-end=\"3144\">Ubiquitin tags damaged proteins for destruction</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>"}, {"id": "6", "question": "৬) Which one participates in mitotic spindle formation during cell division?", "option1": "Centrosome", "option2": "Proteasomes", "option3": "lysosome", "option4": "peroxisome", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p data-start=\"3306\" data-end=\"3454\" class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\">The correct answer is<span> </span><strong data-start=\"3328\" data-end=\"3342\">centrosome</strong>. Centrosomes contain centrioles and act as the<span> </span><strong data-start=\"3390\" data-end=\"3423\">microtubule-organizing center</strong><span> </span>for mitotic spindle formation.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3456\" data-end=\"3581\">\r\n<li data-start=\"3456\" data-end=\"3496\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3458\" data-end=\"3496\"><strong data-start=\"3458\" data-end=\"3473\">Proteasomes</strong><span> </span>– Protein degradation.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3497\" data-end=\"3539\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3499\" data-end=\"3539\"><strong data-start=\"3499\" data-end=\"3512\">Lysosomes</strong><span> </span>– Intracellular digestion.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3540\" data-end=\"3581\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3542\" data-end=\"3581\"><strong data-start=\"3542\" data-end=\"3557\">Peroxisomes</strong><span> </span>– Oxidative metabolism.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"3583\" data-end=\"3605\"><strong data-start=\"3583\" data-end=\"3605\">High-yield points:</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3606\" data-end=\"3650\">\r\n<li data-start=\"3606\" data-end=\"3650\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3608\" data-end=\"3650\"><strong data-start=\"3608\" data-end=\"3650\">Centrosome → Mitotic spindle formation</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>"}, {"id": "7", "question": "৭) Which is the process of uptake of dissolved substances?", "option1": "Endocytosis", "option2": "Exocytosis", "option3": "Pinocytosis", "option4": "Phagocytosis", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p data-start=\"3795\" data-end=\"3925\" class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\">The correct answer is<span> </span><strong data-start=\"3817\" data-end=\"3832\">pinocytosis</strong>. Pinocytosis is the uptake of<span> </span><strong data-start=\"3863\" data-end=\"3897\">fluid and dissolved substances</strong><span> </span>by cells (\"cell drinking\").</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3927\" data-end=\"4118\">\r\n<li data-start=\"3927\" data-end=\"3998\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3929\" data-end=\"3998\"><strong data-start=\"3929\" data-end=\"3944\">Endocytosis</strong><span> </span>– General process of bringing material into the cell.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3999\" data-end=\"4054\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4001\" data-end=\"4054\"><strong data-start=\"4001\" data-end=\"4015\">Exocytosis</strong><span> </span>– Release of substances from the cell.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4055\" data-end=\"4118\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4057\" data-end=\"4118\"><strong data-start=\"4057\" data-end=\"4073\">Phagocytosis</strong><span> </span>– Uptake of large particles (\"cell eating\").</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"4120\" data-end=\"4142\"><strong data-start=\"4120\" data-end=\"4142\">High-yield points:</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4143\" data-end=\"4218\">\r\n<li data-start=\"4143\" data-end=\"4175\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4145\" data-end=\"4175\"><strong data-start=\"4145\" data-end=\"4175\">Pinocytosis → Fluid uptake</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4176\" data-end=\"4218\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4178\" data-end=\"4218\"><strong data-start=\"4178\" data-end=\"4218\">Phagocytosis → Solid particle uptake</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>"}, {"id": "8", "question": "৮) Which is the longest part of cell cycle?", "option1": "G0 phase", "option2": "G1 phase", "option3": "G2 phase", "option4": "S phase", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p data-start=\"4347\" data-end=\"4514\" class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\">The correct answer is<span> </span><strong data-start=\"4369\" data-end=\"4381\">G1 phase</strong>. G1 is usually the longest phase of the cell cycle, involving cell growth, organelle synthesis, and preparation for DNA replication.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4516\" data-end=\"4634\">\r\n<li data-start=\"4516\" data-end=\"4567\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4518\" data-end=\"4567\"><strong data-start=\"4518\" data-end=\"4524\">G0</strong><span> </span>– Resting phase outside active cell cycle.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4568\" data-end=\"4603\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4570\" data-end=\"4603\"><strong data-start=\"4570\" data-end=\"4576\">G2</strong><span> </span>– Preparation for mitosis.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4604\" data-end=\"4634\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4606\" data-end=\"4634\"><strong data-start=\"4606\" data-end=\"4617\">S phase</strong><span> </span>– DNA synthesis.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"4636\" data-end=\"4658\"><strong data-start=\"4636\" data-end=\"4658\">High-yield points:</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4659\" data-end=\"4727\">\r\n<li data-start=\"4659\" data-end=\"4683\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4661\" data-end=\"4683\"><strong data-start=\"4661\" data-end=\"4683\">G1 → Longest phase</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4684\" data-end=\"4709\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4686\" data-end=\"4709\"><strong data-start=\"4686\" data-end=\"4709\">S → DNA replication</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4710\" data-end=\"4727\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4712\" data-end=\"4727\"><strong data-start=\"4712\" data-end=\"4727\">M → Mitosis</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>"}, {"id": "9", "question": "৯) Inactive chromatin stains more darkly and is called......?", "option1": "euchromatin", "option2": "heterochromatin", "option3": "lethal chromatin", "option4": "nonsense chromatin", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p data-start=\"4879\" data-end=\"4999\" class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\">The correct answer is<span> </span><strong data-start=\"4901\" data-end=\"4920\">heterochromatin</strong>. It is tightly packed, transcriptionally inactive chromatin and stains darkly.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"5001\" data-end=\"5065\">\r\n<li data-start=\"5001\" data-end=\"5065\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5003\" data-end=\"5065\"><strong data-start=\"5003\" data-end=\"5018\">Euchromatin</strong><span> </span>– Loosely packed and transcriptionally active.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"5067\" data-end=\"5089\"><strong data-start=\"5067\" data-end=\"5089\">High-yield points:</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"5090\" data-end=\"5190\">\r\n<li data-start=\"5090\" data-end=\"5135\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5092\" data-end=\"5135\"><strong data-start=\"5092\" data-end=\"5135\">Heterochromatin → Dark stain + inactive</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"5136\" data-end=\"5190\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5138\" data-end=\"5190\"><strong data-start=\"5138\" data-end=\"5190\">Euchromatin → Light stain + active transcription</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>"}, {"id": "10", "question": "১০) Which organelle is responsible for sequestration and controlled release of calcium ions?", "option1": "rough endoplasmic reticulum", "option2": "smooth endoplasmic reticulum", "option3": "centriole", "option4": "intermediate filament", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p data-start=\"5388\" data-end=\"5549\" class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\">The correct answer is<span> </span><strong data-start=\"5410\" data-end=\"5448\">smooth endoplasmic reticulum (SER)</strong>. SER stores and releases calcium ions, especially in muscle cells as the<span> </span><strong data-start=\"5522\" data-end=\"5548\">sarcoplasmic reticulum</strong>.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"5551\" data-end=\"5669\">\r\n<li data-start=\"5551\" data-end=\"5586\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5553\" data-end=\"5586\"><strong data-start=\"5553\" data-end=\"5565\">Rough ER</strong><span> </span>– Protein synthesis.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"5587\" data-end=\"5619\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5589\" data-end=\"5619\"><strong data-start=\"5589\" data-end=\"5602\">Centriole</strong><span> </span>– Cell division.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"5620\" data-end=\"5669\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5622\" data-end=\"5669\"><strong data-start=\"5622\" data-end=\"5647\">Intermediate filament</strong><span> </span>– Structural support.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"5671\" data-end=\"5693\"><strong data-start=\"5671\" data-end=\"5693\">High-yield points:</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"5694\" data-end=\"5736\">\r\n<li data-start=\"5694\" data-end=\"5736\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5696\" data-end=\"5736\"><strong data-start=\"5696\" data-end=\"5736\">SER → Lipid synthesis + Ca²⁺ storage</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>"}, {"id": "11", "question": "১১) Which of the following Propels sperm?", "option1": "Cilia", "option2": "Flagellum", "option3": "Microvilli", "option4": "Stereocilia", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p data-start=\"5862\" data-end=\"5964\" class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\">The correct answer is<span> </span><strong data-start=\"5884\" data-end=\"5897\">flagellum</strong>. The sperm tail is a specialized flagellum that provides motility.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"5966\" data-end=\"6116\">\r\n<li data-start=\"5966\" data-end=\"6021\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5968\" data-end=\"6021\"><strong data-start=\"5968\" data-end=\"5977\">Cilia</strong><span> </span>– Move substances over epithelial surfaces.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"6022\" data-end=\"6063\">\r\n<p data-start=\"6024\" data-end=\"6063\"><strong data-start=\"6024\" data-end=\"6038\">Microvilli</strong><span> </span>– Increase surface area.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"6064\" data-end=\"6116\">\r\n<p data-start=\"6066\" data-end=\"6116\"><strong data-start=\"6066\" data-end=\"6081\">Stereocilia</strong><span> </span>– Long microvilli-like structures.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"6118\" data-end=\"6140\"><strong data-start=\"6118\" data-end=\"6140\">High-yield points:</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"6141\" data-end=\"6173\">\r\n<li data-start=\"6141\" data-end=\"6173\">\r\n<p data-start=\"6143\" data-end=\"6173\"><strong data-start=\"6143\" data-end=\"6173\">Sperm movement → Flagellum</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>"}, {"id": "12", "question": "১২) Which one is start codon?", "option1": "UAG", "option2": "AUG", "option3": "UAA", "option4": "UGA", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p data-start=\"6281\" data-end=\"6371\" class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\">The correct answer is<span> </span><strong data-start=\"6303\" data-end=\"6310\">AUG</strong>. AUG is the universal<span> </span><strong data-start=\"6333\" data-end=\"6348\">start codon</strong><span> </span>coding for methionine.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"6373\" data-end=\"6407\">\r\n<li data-start=\"6373\" data-end=\"6407\">\r\n<p data-start=\"6375\" data-end=\"6407\"><strong data-start=\"6375\" data-end=\"6392\">UAG, UAA, UGA</strong><span> </span>– Stop codons.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"6409\" data-end=\"6431\"><strong data-start=\"6409\" data-end=\"6431\">High-yield points:</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"6432\" data-end=\"6489\">\r\n<li data-start=\"6432\" data-end=\"6455\">\r\n<p data-start=\"6434\" data-end=\"6455\"><strong data-start=\"6434\" data-end=\"6455\">Start codon → AUG</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"6456\" data-end=\"6489\">\r\n<p data-start=\"6458\" data-end=\"6489\"><strong data-start=\"6458\" data-end=\"6489\">Stop codons → UAA, UAG, UGA</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>"}, {"id": "13", "question": "১৩) The nuclear envelope is supported internally by a meshwork called lamins which is composed of......?", "option1": "microtubule", "option2": "microfilament", "option3": "intermediate filament", "option4": "golgi apparatus", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p data-start=\"6671\" data-end=\"6836\" class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\">The correct answer is<span> </span><strong data-start=\"6693\" data-end=\"6718\">intermediate filament</strong>. Nuclear lamins are a specialized type of intermediate filament providing structural support to the nuclear envelope.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6838\" data-end=\"6860\"><strong data-start=\"6838\" data-end=\"6860\">High-yield points:</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"6861\" data-end=\"6906\">\r\n<li data-start=\"6861\" data-end=\"6906\">\r\n<p data-start=\"6863\" data-end=\"6906\"><strong data-start=\"6863\" data-end=\"6906\">Lamins → Intermediate filament proteins</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>"}, {"id": "14", "question": "১৪) Stereocilia is present in......?", "option1": "spermatozoa", "option2": "ductus deferens", "option3": "renal tubules", "option4": "intestine", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p data-start=\"7035\" data-end=\"7166\" class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\">The correct answer is<span> </span><strong data-start=\"7057\" data-end=\"7076\">ductus deferens</strong>. Stereocilia are long, non-motile microvilli found in the epididymis and ductus deferens.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"7168\" data-end=\"7252\">\r\n<li data-start=\"7168\" data-end=\"7203\">\r\n<p data-start=\"7170\" data-end=\"7203\"><strong data-start=\"7170\" data-end=\"7185\">Spermatozoa</strong><span> </span>– Have flagellum.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"7204\" data-end=\"7252\">\r\n<p data-start=\"7206\" data-end=\"7252\"><strong data-start=\"7206\" data-end=\"7233\">Renal tubules/intestine</strong><span> </span>– Have microvilli.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"7254\" data-end=\"7276\"><strong data-start=\"7254\" data-end=\"7276\">High-yield points:</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"7277\" data-end=\"7325\">\r\n<li data-start=\"7277\" data-end=\"7325\">\r\n<p data-start=\"7279\" data-end=\"7325\"><strong data-start=\"7279\" data-end=\"7325\">Stereocilia → Epididymis + ductus deferens</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>"}, {"id": "15", "question": "১৫) Which organelle act as sites of intracellular digestion and turnover of cellular components?", "option1": "ribosome", "option2": "lysosome", "option3": "peroxisome", "option4": "centrosome", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p data-start=\"7506\" data-end=\"7621\" class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\">The correct answer is<span> </span><strong data-start=\"7528\" data-end=\"7540\">lysosome</strong>. Lysosomes contain hydrolytic enzymes for intracellular digestion and autophagy.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7623\" data-end=\"7645\"><strong data-start=\"7623\" data-end=\"7645\">High-yield points:</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"7646\" data-end=\"7686\">\r\n<li data-start=\"7646\" data-end=\"7686\">\r\n<p data-start=\"7648\" data-end=\"7686\"><strong data-start=\"7648\" data-end=\"7686\">Lysosome → Intracellular digestion</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>"}, {"id": "16", "question": "১৬) In which phase of meiosis-1 bivalent occurs?", "option1": "leptotene", "option2": "zygotene", "option3": "pachytene", "option4": "diplotene", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p data-start=\"7820\" data-end=\"7944\" class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\">The correct answer is<span> </span><strong data-start=\"7842\" data-end=\"7854\">zygotene</strong>. During zygotene, homologous chromosomes pair together by synapsis forming<span> </span><strong data-start=\"7930\" data-end=\"7943\">bivalents</strong>.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"7946\" data-end=\"8079\">\r\n<li data-start=\"7946\" data-end=\"7985\">\r\n<p data-start=\"7948\" data-end=\"7985\"><strong data-start=\"7948\" data-end=\"7961\">Pachytene</strong><span> </span>– Crossing over occurs.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"7986\" data-end=\"8029\">\r\n<p data-start=\"7988\" data-end=\"8029\"><strong data-start=\"7988\" data-end=\"8001\">Diplotene</strong><span> </span>– Chiasmata become visible.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"8030\" data-end=\"8079\">\r\n<p data-start=\"8032\" data-end=\"8079\"><strong data-start=\"8032\" data-end=\"8045\">Leptotene</strong><span> </span>– Chromosomes begin condensation.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"8081\" data-end=\"8103\"><strong data-start=\"8081\" data-end=\"8103\">High-yield points:</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"8104\" data-end=\"8182\">\r\n<li data-start=\"8104\" data-end=\"8150\">\r\n<p data-start=\"8106\" data-end=\"8150\"><strong data-start=\"8106\" data-end=\"8150\">Zygotene → Synapsis + bivalent formation</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"8151\" data-end=\"8182\">\r\n<p data-start=\"8153\" data-end=\"8182\"><strong data-start=\"8153\" data-end=\"8182\">Pachytene → Crossing over</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>"}, {"id": "17", "question": "১৭) Which of the following is not a criteria of mitosis cell division?", "option1": "chromosomes are not visible", "option2": "prophase short", "option3": "interphase short", "option4": "occurs in somatic cells", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p data-start=\"8338\" data-end=\"8464\" class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\">The correct answer is<span> </span><strong data-start=\"8360\" data-end=\"8391\">chromosomes are not visible</strong>. During mitosis, chromosomes become clearly visible due to condensation.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"8466\" data-end=\"8579\">\r\n<li data-start=\"8466\" data-end=\"8500\">\r\n<p data-start=\"8468\" data-end=\"8500\">Mitosis occurs in somatic cells.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"8501\" data-end=\"8532\">\r\n<p data-start=\"8503\" data-end=\"8532\">Prophase is relatively short.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"8533\" data-end=\"8579\">\r\n<p data-start=\"8535\" data-end=\"8579\">Interphase before mitosis is usually longer.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"8581\" data-end=\"8603\"><strong data-start=\"8581\" data-end=\"8603\">High-yield points:</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"8604\" data-end=\"8655\">\r\n<li data-start=\"8604\" data-end=\"8655\">\r\n<p data-start=\"8606\" data-end=\"8655\"><strong data-start=\"8606\" data-end=\"8655\">Mitosis → Somatic cells + visible chromosomes</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>"}, {"id": "18", "question": "১৮) Tetrad formation occurs in which stage of cell division?", "option1": "Zygotene", "option2": "Pachytene", "option3": "Diplotene", "option4": "Leptotene", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p data-start=\"8802\" data-end=\"8964\" class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\">The correct answer is<span> </span><strong data-start=\"8824\" data-end=\"8837\">pachytene</strong>. During pachytene of prophase I, homologous chromosomes consist of four chromatids forming a tetrad, and crossing over occurs.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8966\" data-end=\"8988\"><strong data-start=\"8966\" data-end=\"8988\">High-yield points:</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"8989\" data-end=\"9029\">\r\n<li data-start=\"8989\" data-end=\"9029\">\r\n<p data-start=\"8991\" data-end=\"9029\"><strong data-start=\"8991\" data-end=\"9029\">Pachytene → Tetrad + crossing over</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>"}, {"id": "19", "question": "১৯) Which one is direct cell division?", "option1": "amitosis", "option2": "mitosis", "option3": "meiosis", "option4": "cytokinesis", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p data-start=\"9151\" data-end=\"9273\" class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\">The correct answer is<span> </span><strong data-start=\"9173\" data-end=\"9185\">amitosis</strong>. Amitosis is direct cell division without spindle formation or chromosome condensation.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"9275\" data-end=\"9410\">\r\n<li data-start=\"9275\" data-end=\"9332\">\r\n<p data-start=\"9277\" data-end=\"9332\"><strong data-start=\"9277\" data-end=\"9288\">Mitosis</strong><span> </span>– Indirect division with spindle formation.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"9333\" data-end=\"9368\">\r\n<p data-start=\"9335\" data-end=\"9368\"><strong data-start=\"9335\" data-end=\"9346\">Meiosis</strong><span> </span>– Reduction division.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"9369\" data-end=\"9410\">\r\n<p data-start=\"9371\" data-end=\"9410\"><strong data-start=\"9371\" data-end=\"9386\">Cytokinesis</strong><span> </span>– Cytoplasmic division.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"9412\" data-end=\"9434\"><strong data-start=\"9412\" data-end=\"9434\">High-yield points:</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"9435\" data-end=\"9472\">\r\n<li data-start=\"9435\" data-end=\"9472\">\r\n<p data-start=\"9437\" data-end=\"9472\"><strong data-start=\"9437\" data-end=\"9472\">Amitosis = Direct cell division</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>"}, {"id": "20", "question": "২০) Which organelle completes post-translational modifications of proteins?", "option1": "rough endoplasmic reticulum", "option2": "smooth endoplasmic reticulum", "option3": "golgi apparatus", "option4": "ribosome", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p data-start=\"9638\" data-end=\"9742\" class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\">The correct answer is<span> </span><strong data-start=\"9660\" data-end=\"9679\">Golgi apparatus</strong>. Golgi modifies, sorts, and packages proteins after synthesis.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"9744\" data-end=\"9872\">\r\n<li data-start=\"9744\" data-end=\"9799\">\r\n<p data-start=\"9746\" data-end=\"9799\"><strong data-start=\"9746\" data-end=\"9758\">Rough ER</strong><span> </span>– Initial protein synthesis and folding.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"9800\" data-end=\"9834\">\r\n<p data-start=\"9802\" data-end=\"9834\"><strong data-start=\"9802\" data-end=\"9815\">Smooth ER</strong><span> </span>– Lipid synthesis.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"9835\" data-end=\"9872\">\r\n<p data-start=\"9837\" data-end=\"9872\"><strong data-start=\"9837\" data-end=\"9849\">Ribosome</strong><span> </span>– Protein translation.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"9874\" data-end=\"9896\"><strong data-start=\"9874\" data-end=\"9896\">High-yield points:</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"9897\" data-end=\"9977\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">\r\n<li data-start=\"9897\" data-end=\"9926\">\r\n<p data-start=\"9899\" data-end=\"9926\"><strong data-start=\"9899\" data-end=\"9926\">RER → Protein synthesis</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"9927\" data-end=\"9977\" data-is-last-node=\"\">\r\n<p data-start=\"9929\" data-end=\"9977\" data-is-last-node=\"\"><strong data-start=\"9929\" data-end=\"9977\" data-is-last-node=\"\">Golgi → Modification + packaging + secretion</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>"}]}, "_source": "archive-question-subject", "_exam_id": 278, "custom_field": "", "exam_time": "420000", "is_omr": false, "omr_time": "7200000", "examname": "May 08, 2018", "type": "BCS-Health-Long", "payment": "BALANCE_NOT"}